
# 2026-10-08 19:26:02.805681
+Align scripts/census.sh (Unix scanner) with scripts/census.ps1 (Windows scanner). Constraints: must run on macOS bash 3.2 and BSD awk (no mapfile, no associative arrays, no ${x,,}, no gawk-only functions); always write ${VAR} (braces) when a variable is followed by a non-ASCII character; no jq/python. Do NOT change the JSON schema (schemaVersion stays 1). Make only these changes:
+1. STRAY warning: currently `add_warn "STRAY" "stray" ...`. census.ps1 sets the tool field to the unique, sorted stray tool names joined with '/' (e.g. `node` or `java/node`). Make census.sh do the same (STRAY_ROWS lines are "tool version @ path"; take field 1, sort -u, join with '/').
+2. Candidate roots: `for r in $CANDIDATE_ROOTS; do probe_root "$r"; done` word-splits roots containing spaces (e.g. '/Applications/Android Studio.app/Contents/jbr', or $HOME with a space). CANDIDATE_ROOTS is newline-separated. Iterate it line by line so spaces are preserved and no globbing happens. probe_root launches child processes that might read stdin, so do NOT feed the loop on stdin; read from fd 3 instead (`while IFS= read -r r <&3; do [ -n "$r" ] || continue; probe_root "$r"; done 3<<EOF ... EOF`) or an equivalent IFS=newline + set -f approach that restores IFS/globbing. Update the comment above it that says the old for loop is kept.
+3. Resolution layer: `for c in $RESOLVE_CMDS $DECLARED_CMDS; do` lists a declared command twice when it is also in the default list. Dedupe (keep first occurrence order, i.e. default list order then new declared commands), like census.ps1 which does -ExtraCommands with unique names.
+4. UNDECLARED warning: census.ps1 counts a project-scope declaration file named mise.toml, .mise.toml, .tool-versions, .nvmrc or .node-version as a project declaration, so no UNDECLARED warning is raised when any of them exists in the project dir. census.sh only checks $PROJECT_DECL_FILES (mise/tool-versions files). Make census.sh also treat .nvmrc / .node-version in the current directory $(pwd) as a project declaration for this UNDECLARED check only (do not add them to DECL_FILES or declared_tools).
+Tests: in tests/smoke.sh add regression checks for items 2-4 using the existing sandbox (keep them small, use plain grep/awk on the JSON output like existing checks): (a) a candidate root containing a space is probed — e.g. create a stray node under a directory with a space that ends up in the candidate roots (look at how candidate roots are built from scripts/census-data.tsv with {HOME} etc.; if no static root can be placed in the sandbox, test with a sandbox HOME-relative root) and assert the JSON contains that path; (b) the resolution array contains each command at most once when a declared tool (e.g. node) is also a default resolve command; (c) running census.sh in a project dir that has package.json with engines.node plus .nvmrc yields no UNDECLARED, while package.json alone yields UNDECLARED. In tests/fixtures/census-expected.tsv change the STRAY row's tool from `*` to the actual stray tool name in the sandbox (node) and delete the comment lines that say STRAY uses * until C4.

# 2026-10-08 19:26:02.858142
+Docs update (Chinese, match the existing style and tone of each file; minimal additions, no rewrites):
+1. docs/contributing.md and docs/reference.md: make clear that adding a new tool / probe location / candidate root / resolve command only requires editing scripts/census-data.tsv (kind<TAB>os<TAB>value, os = all/win/unix) and, for any new user-facing text, scripts/census-text.tsv (key<TAB>lang<TAB>text, zh and en both required); census.ps1 and census.sh both read these, no script edits needed. Mention that census-text.tsv no longer has ps1:/sh: prefixed keys: platform differences (like the bootstrap script name) live in census-data.tsv as os=win/unix rows and are passed to text as placeholders.
+2. docs/platform-notes.md: add notes that (a) on Windows PowerShell 5.1 the probe-timeout cleanup uses `taskkill /T /F` as best effort because .NET Framework has no native process-tree kill (PowerShell 7 uses Kill($true)); if taskkill fails only the direct child is killed; (b) `map.ps1 scan -Throttle 1` (also setup) gives the old serial scan; (c) the PATH_DIRT check for quoted PATH entries is Windows-only (quotes in PATH entries are a Windows-specific mistake); duplicates/missing directories are checked on both platforms; (d) census.sh reports mise tools from plain `mise ls` text (tool/version/requested) without installPath because parsing `mise ls --json` portably needs jq, which census.sh avoids.

# 2026-10-08 19:26:02.960753
+In scripts/census.ps1 fix the PowerShell version probe. Get-NormalizedVersion has `'powershell'` and `'pwsh'` switch branches that call Get-FirstLine $ExePath ... (ExePath is not even a parameter there; it leaks via dynamic scope), assign $raw and then fall out of the switch returning nothing, so the version is always null and a process launch is wasted. Fix: in Get-RuntimeVersion add one branch for 'powershell' and 'pwsh' that probes once with Get-FirstLine $ExePath @('-NoProfile', '-NonInteractive', '-Command', '$PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString()') (powershell.exe does not support --version, so these two must not fall into the default --version/-version/version chain). In Get-NormalizedVersion replace the two broken branches with a single 'powershell'/'pwsh' branch that only extracts the version with the regex '([0-9]+\.[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)*)' from $Raw (no process launch). Keep function names, parameters and locations unchanged; keep the file's UTF-8 BOM and line endings; minimal diff.

# 2026-10-08 19:33:06.774126
+Two tasks. Use minimal SEARCH/REPLACE edits.
+TASK 1 (scripts/census.ps1): fix the PowerShell version probe. Get-NormalizedVersion has 'powershell' and 'pwsh' switch branches that call Get-FirstLine $ExePath (ExePath is not a parameter there), assign $raw and fall out of the switch returning nothing: version is always empty and a process launch is wasted. Fix: in Get-RuntimeVersion add one branch `{ $_ -in 'powershell', 'pwsh' }` (or two labels) that probes once: $raw = Get-FirstLine $ExePath @('-NoProfile', '-NonInteractive', '-Command', '$PSVersionTable.PSVersion.ToString()') — these must not fall into the default --version/-version/version chain. In Get-NormalizedVersion replace the two broken branches with a branch for 'powershell'/'pwsh' that only extracts '([0-9]+\.[0-9]+(?:\.[0-9]+)*)' from $Raw (return $Raw if no match). Keep function names/locations.
+TASK 2: remove the `ps1:` / `sh:` key-prefix override mechanism from scripts/census-text.tsv and unify the wording:
+- warn.PATH_DIRT.message becomes one unprefixed key (zh+en): zh `PATH 里有{parts}。它们不改变解析结果，但会挤占 PATH 长度（Windows 有上限），并让「改了却没生效」这类问题更难查。` en `PATH contains {parts}. They do not change resolution, but they use up PATH length (Windows has a limit) and hide “I changed it but nothing took effect” problems.`
+- The bootstrap script name is a genuine platform difference: add rows to scripts/census-data.tsv: kind `bootstrap` os win value `scripts/bootstrap.ps1`; kind `bootstrap` os unix value `scripts/bootstrap.sh`; kind `bootstrap-refresh` os win value `scripts/bootstrap.ps1 -RefreshConfig`; kind `bootstrap-refresh` os unix value `scripts/bootstrap.sh --refresh-config` (follow the file's existing comment/section conventions). Both scripts already load census-data.tsv by kind/os (find the existing helper in each: in census.sh data_list, in census.ps1 the equivalent); read these single values once.
+- Unprefixed text keys (zh+en): warn.DRIFT.action zh `刷新: {refresh}（会先备份）` en `Refresh it: {refresh} (backs up first)`; warn.MISSING.action zh `执行 mise install 把它装上（新机器可直接跑 {bootstrap}）` en `Install it with mise install (on a new machine, just run {bootstrap})`; warn.NO_MISE.action zh `执行 {bootstrap} 建立声明式层` en `Run {bootstrap} to set up the declarative layer`. Delete all ps1:/sh: rows and update the header comment of census-text.tsv (no prefixes anymore).
+- Pass the facts: in census.ps1 New-Warning calls for DRIFT, MISSING, NO_MISE add bootstrap/refresh to -Facts (or have New-Warning merge them in for every warning); in census.sh add_warn calls for DRIFT, MISSING, NO_MISE add "bootstrap=..." / "refresh=..." key=value args (look how add_warn passes "key=value" to T). Make sure these extra facts do not change the JSON `facts` shape in a way tests reject — if facts are emitted to JSON that is fine (additive) but keep schemaVersion 1.
+- Remove the prefix handling code from the text loaders: census.ps1 (around `$key.StartsWith('sh:')` / `ps1:` override) and census.sh (the awk lookup with `$1 == "sh:" k` priorities; keep current-lang > any-lang fallback) and their comments.
+- tests/check-text.ps1: anything that handles/permits ps1:/sh: prefixes should now reject any key containing ':' prefix `ps1:`/`sh:` (fail with a clear message). tests/check-data.ps1: allow the new kinds `bootstrap` and `bootstrap-refresh` and require both win and unix rows for each.
+Constraints: census.sh must run on bash 3.2 + BSD awk; always ${VAR} with braces before non-ASCII characters; .ps1 files keep their UTF-8 BOM; .tsv files are TAB separated with LF.

